<title>JAPAN: Japan May department store sales down 5.1 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>Japan May department store sales down 5.1 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales at department stores in Japan in May declined 5.1 percent from a year earlier to 658.9 billion yen, the Japan Department Stores' Association said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Overall sales showed signs of recovery in May but sales of large and expensive items were slow due to a reaction to increased demand for such products ahead of a rise in the sales tax on April 1, the association said in a statement.</p>
<p>The negative impact of the tax increase on individual customers was smaller in May than in April but purchases by corporate customers remained sluggish, it said.</p>
<p>The survey covered 263 outlets of 108 companies.</p>
</text>
